WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.299
Module eight. Payouts, disputes, and what's still pending.

2
00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:09.828
This is the last module. After this, you'll take the quiz.

3
00:00:10.278 --> 00:00:12.561
We'll read a payout in Earnings and Settlements.

4
00:00:13.011 --> 00:00:15.080
See how to raise and handle a dispute.

5
00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:17.343
Look at vendor settings and support.

6
00:00:17.793 --> 00:00:20.311
Understand how customers see prices today.

7
00:00:20.761 --> 00:00:24.686
And finish with what's pending, common questions, and a final recap.

8
00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:30.241
In the vendor console, open Earnings and Settlements.

9
00:00:30.241 --> 00:00:31.900
At the top are four numbers.

10
00:00:32.350 --> 00:00:36.147
Total settled payout: all the money already paid out to the vendor.

11
00:00:36.597 --> 00:00:38.795
Next payout: the upcoming settlement.

12
00:00:39.245 --> 00:00:43.490
Deductions: what Oribrix deducts, which is logistics plus commission.

13
00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:47.097
And open disputes: tickets that are still under review.

14
00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:52.913
Below is the settlements table. Each row is one payout.

15
00:00:52.913 --> 00:00:54.279
Here's how to read it.

16
00:00:54.729 --> 00:00:59.337
The settlement ID. If there's ever a problem, quote this ID in the dispute.

17
00:00:59.787 --> 00:01:02.069
The date, and how many orders are included.

18
00:01:02.519 --> 00:01:05.143
GMV, the total value of those orders.

19
00:01:05.593 --> 00:01:07.065
The GST portion.

20
00:01:07.515 --> 00:01:10.182
Deductions, which are logistics plus commission.

21
00:01:10.632 --> 00:01:15.280
And the payout amount, with its status: settled, or Tally synced once it's in

22
00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:15.944
Accounting.

23
00:01:18.333 --> 00:01:21.910
Let's walk through one payout with simple example numbers.

24
00:01:21.910 --> 00:01:25.117
These are not real rates, just to show how it works.

25
00:01:25.567 --> 00:01:29.473
Say the orders in this settlement are worth ten thousand rupees.

26
00:01:29.473 --> 00:01:30.388
That's the GMV.

27
00:01:30.838 --> 00:01:36.065
Oribrix deducts logistics and commission. In this example, six hundred rupees.

28
00:01:36.515 --> 00:01:41.749
So the payout is nine thousand four hundred rupees, sent to the bank account from

29
00:01:41.749 --> 00:01:45.368
The KYC. That's why correct bank details matter so much.

30
00:01:47.767 --> 00:01:49.687
Let's watch this in the live demo.

31
00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:58.079
Here is Earnings and Settlements, with the four numbers at the top, and tabs for

32
00:01:58.079 --> 00:01:59.281
Payouts and disputes.

33
00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:13.585
The vendor's warehouses page now shows two approved warehouses, both in Lucknow.

34
00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:39.822
The settlements table lists each payout. There are buttons to export Tally XML and

35
00:02:39.822 --> 00:02:42.044
CSV, for the vendor's accountant.

36
00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:07.256
The team confirmed that returns, disputes, KYC and settings are working.

37
00:03:07.256 --> 00:03:11.111
Settings let vendors reset their password and add staff.

38
00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:37.119
If a vendor thinks a payout is wrong, they raise a dispute.

39
00:03:37.119 --> 00:03:40.860
A dispute is a conversation between the vendor and the admin.

40
00:03:41.310 --> 00:03:42.931
Go to Earnings and Settlements.

41
00:03:43.381 --> 00:03:45.941
Open disputes, and click Create new dispute.

42
00:03:46.391 --> 00:03:50.402
In the subject, write the settlement ID, or the missing order ID.

43
00:03:50.852 --> 00:03:55.033
Explain the issue in detail, and attach proof, like a proof of delivery.

44
00:03:55.483 --> 00:03:58.129
Submit. The admin will reply in the same thread.

45
00:04:00.533 --> 00:04:02.453
Let's watch this in the live demo.

46
00:04:06.267 --> 00:04:09.915
The disputes tab. Create new dispute opens a small form.

47
00:04:25.467 --> 00:04:30.886
Subject, with the settlement or missing ID. A box to explain the issue in detail.

48
00:04:30.886 --> 00:04:32.358
And a file attachment.

49
00:04:49.467 --> 00:04:55.240
The team also asked for standard formats for vendor, customer, staff and settlement

50
00:04:55.240 --> 00:04:59.622
IDs. Right now IDs are random, so a standard format is pending.

51
00:05:25.467 --> 00:05:29.499
A good dispute gets solved quickly. Teach vendors to include these.

52
00:05:29.949 --> 00:05:32.680
The exact settlement ID or order ID.

53
00:05:33.130 --> 00:05:35.647
What's wrong, in one or two clear sentences.

54
00:05:36.097 --> 00:05:39.020
The amount they expected, and the amount they received.

55
00:05:39.470 --> 00:05:43.032
And proof, like a proof of delivery, an invoice, or a screenshot.

56
00:05:45.433 --> 00:05:47.822
A few more things vendors will ask you about.

57
00:05:48.272 --> 00:05:50.256
Passwords can be reset from Settings.

58
00:05:50.706 --> 00:05:54.824
Vendors can add staff accounts for their team, so they don't share one login.

59
00:05:55.274 --> 00:06:00.458
Optional KYC documents can be uploaded any time from the KYC section.

60
00:06:00.908 --> 00:06:05.768
Data deletion requests go to support. At the time of the session, they were routed

61
00:06:05.768 --> 00:06:09.740
To the developer's address, and are being moved to Oribrix support.

62
00:06:10.190 --> 00:06:14.717
And WhatsApp support access details were still being confirmed with the development

63
00:06:14.717 --> 00:06:14.990
Team.

64
00:06:17.399 --> 00:06:22.258
A big question came up in the session. What if several vendors sell the same product

65
00:06:22.258 --> 00:06:23.415
At different prices?

66
00:06:23.865 --> 00:06:28.553
Today, the app shows the nearest vendor's product and price, so the customer sees

67
00:06:28.553 --> 00:06:30.116
One price per product card.

68
00:06:30.566 --> 00:06:35.847
Under discussion: showing other vendors' prices too, with vendor or warehouse names,

69
00:06:35.847 --> 00:06:41.128
A bit like other quick commerce apps. This matters in markets where many sellers sit

70
00:06:41.128 --> 00:06:44.838
In the same lane. The development team is preparing a plan.

71
00:06:47.233 --> 00:06:50.973
As of the thirteenth of November, these items were still pending.

72
00:06:50.973 --> 00:06:53.505
Some may be done by the time you watch this.

73
00:06:53.955 --> 00:06:57.496
The category name display bug, which showed object object.

74
00:06:57.946 --> 00:07:00.656
Adding the unit field to the CSV template.

75
00:07:01.106 --> 00:07:03.047
The same city price validation.

76
00:07:03.497 --> 00:07:05.374
The Shiprocket express API.

77
00:07:05.824 --> 00:07:08.278
Connecting Tally to the live cloud ID.

78
00:07:08.728 --> 00:07:12.973
Standard formats for vendor, customer, staff and settlement IDs.

79
00:07:13.423 --> 00:07:16.026
A plan to show prices from multiple vendors.

80
00:07:16.476 --> 00:07:18.758
And a full admin panel walkthrough session.

81
00:07:21.166 --> 00:07:25.049
Here are the five questions vendors ask most, with the short answers.

82
00:07:25.499 --> 00:07:31.202
I submitted KYC, when can I sell? After admin approval, usually within twenty four

83
00:07:31.202 --> 00:07:34.053
Hours, and after the final approval step.

84
00:07:34.503 --> 00:07:39.901
Can I add my own product? No. Ask the admin team to add it to the master catalog.

85
00:07:40.351 --> 00:07:45.224
My product isn't showing. Check stock, warehouse approval, the map pin, and whether

86
00:07:45.224 --> 00:07:46.516
The product is active.

87
00:07:46.966 --> 00:07:50.785
Can I sell cheaper? Yes, request a price change with a reason.

88
00:07:51.235 --> 00:07:55.629
My payout looks wrong. Raise a dispute with the settlement ID and proof.

89
00:07:58.032 --> 00:08:01.566
Here's one checklist that brings the whole course together.

90
00:08:01.566 --> 00:08:04.560
Use it to decide if a new vendor is ready to sell.

91
00:08:05.010 --> 00:08:08.679
KYC is approved, including the final approval step.

92
00:08:09.129 --> 00:08:12.265
The warehouse is approved, and verified in Shiprocket.

93
00:08:12.715 --> 00:08:14.934
SKUs are added, with real stock.

94
00:08:15.384 --> 00:08:18.691
Prices are checked, and any price requests are decided.

95
00:08:19.141 --> 00:08:22.170
The vendor can log in, and staff are added if needed.

96
00:08:22.620 --> 00:08:26.396
And local drivers are added as a backup. This one is optional.

97
00:08:28.799 --> 00:08:31.423
Let's finish with the eight rules from this whole course.

98
00:08:31.873 --> 00:08:34.156
One. Only the admin creates products.

99
00:08:34.606 --> 00:08:39.832
Two. The GSTIN must be valid and unique, and the login email must be new.

100
00:08:40.282 --> 00:08:43.205
Three. Final vendor approval is a separate step.

101
00:08:43.655 --> 00:08:47.111
Four. No seller in an approved warehouse means no listing.

102
00:08:47.561 --> 00:08:51.124
Five. Editing a warehouse location sends it back to pending.

103
00:08:51.574 --> 00:08:56.695
Six. Approved prices are for one vendor and one warehouse, and the same city means

104
00:08:56.695 --> 00:08:57.632
The same price.

105
00:08:58.082 --> 00:09:00.941
Seven. Verify every warehouse in Shiprocket.

106
00:09:01.391 --> 00:09:04.527
Eight. In disputes, always quote the settlement ID.

107
00:09:06.932 --> 00:09:09.279
Finally, what does all this mean for your role?

108
00:09:09.729 --> 00:09:14.294
If you're an onboarding executive, help vendors fill the form right the first time.

109
00:09:14.744 --> 00:09:19.544
If you review KYC, check every document, and never skip final approval.

110
00:09:19.994 --> 00:09:25.114
If you manage the catalog, use clear names, and the right GST, unit and weight.

111
00:09:25.564 --> 00:09:29.660
In operations, own Shiprocket verification and dispatch issues.

112
00:09:30.110 --> 00:09:34.490
In support, you'll handle product visibility, payouts and disputes, using the

113
00:09:34.490 --> 00:09:36.083
Checklists from this course.

114
00:09:36.533 --> 00:09:40.395
And for everyone: follow the rules, and when you're unsure, escalate.

115
00:09:42.799 --> 00:09:45.124
You've finished all eight modules. Well done.

116
00:09:45.574 --> 00:09:49.350
Now take the quiz. You get only one attempt, so take your time.

117
00:09:49.800 --> 00:09:52.190
After the quiz, download your certificate.

118
00:09:52.640 --> 00:09:56.458
Keep this course link, and come back to any module whenever you need it.

119
00:09:56.908 --> 00:10:00.313
And if you have questions, ask your Oribrix team lead.

120
00:10:00.313 --> 00:10:03.970
Thank you, and welcome to Oribrix. Order now, build today.

121
00:10:06.366 --> 00:10:10.109
That's the end of module 8. You've completed all eight modules.

122
00:10:10.109 --> 00:10:12.723
Now take the quiz, and get your certificate.
